  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Tally marks and equal classes"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "To build a frequency distribution, decide the classes, then read each value and put a tally mark against its class. Every fifth tally is drawn across the previous four, making bundles of five. Count the tallies to get frequencies. Classes are usually of equal width; the number of classes is about range divided by width.",
    "kn": "ಪ್ರತಿ ಮೌಲ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಅದರ ವರ್ಗದ ಎದುರು ಗಣನಾ ಗುರುತು ಹಾಕಿ. ಐದನೇ ಗುರುತು ಹಿಂದಿನ ನಾಲ್ಕರ ಮೇಲೆ ಅಡ್ಡವಾಗಿ. ಗುರುತುಗಳನ್ನು ಎಣಿಸಿ ಆವರ್ತನ ಪಡೆಯಿರಿ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Range = largest value − smallest value"
    },
    {
     "en": "Number of classes ≈ range ÷ class width"
    },
    {
     "en": "Tallies are grouped in fives"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "To build a frequency distribution, decide the classes, then read each value and put a tally mark against its class. Every fifth tally is drawn across the previous four, making bundles of five. Count the tallies to get frequencies. Classes are usually of equal width; the number of classes is about range divided by width.",
    "kn": "ಪ್ರತಿ ಮೌಲ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಅದರ ವರ್ಗದ ಎದುರು ಗಣನಾ ಗುರುತು ಹಾಕಿ. ಐದನೇ ಗುರುತು ಹಿಂದಿನ ನಾಲ್ಕರ ಮೇಲೆ ಅಡ್ಡವಾಗಿ. ಗುರುತುಗಳನ್ನು ಎಣಿಸಿ ಆವರ್ತನ ಪಡೆಯಿರಿ."
   }
